WEBVTT

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:16.750
He means we must stay here.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:20.460
The door's been locked.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.210
I don't understand the criteria.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:27.590
He's definitely watching how we
fulfill our role as a shadow face.

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:31.390
But why was Ricky demoted one rank?

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:33.600
What was the reason behind your demotion?

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.970
Enough, already!

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.890
We weren't told to dance.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:39.560
So it's my fault for
taking the initiative?

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.440
You all danced, so you're just as guilty!

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:46.020
It probably all hinges on how
Edward feels at the moment.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.490
That's so unfair!

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:51.160
We are living dolls.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:55.030
The Shadows family may
treat us however they see fit.

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:57.870
Aren't you fretting
over trivial matters, Ricky?

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.410
You're one to talk!

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:38.050
What's taking so long?
Are we supposed to go, too?

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:39.130
THE GARDEN LABYRINTH

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:42.980
Don't be stupid. It's locked,
and he didn't tell us to come along.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:44.980
Use your brain, Black Sheep.

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:46.980
He never said we shouldn't come!

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:49.650
But that's what he meant!

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.740
Please don't fight!

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:05.540
This is why they call you Sunshine.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:07.460
We're bitter rivals.

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:10.960
And why in the world do
you hold your cup like that?

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:14.340
How sorry I feel for Kate.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:18.050
You hold cups by their handle.

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:20.390
Elegant, right?

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:22.810
No one holds it in both hands.

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:25.390
Oh, Ricky!

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:28.650
Thank you for telling me!

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:35.690
Emilico! You're just some
unloved doll with a strange name!

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:41.200
Mistress Kate told me
I was fine just how I am.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:45.660
And I have no right or
reason to not believe her.

00:03:57.010 --> 00:04:00.840
Th-That's disgusting!
You're trying to mock me!

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.550
Huh?

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:03.760
A stone?

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:07.850
You fool! That's what you get
for thinking it was okay to eat!

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:10.060
It's more of Edward's abuse.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:12.980
Hm? Where have I seen this before?

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:16.070
Oh, that's a <i>fève</i>. I read about them.

00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:18.700
It's a small porcelain good luck charm.

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:23.280
One is placed inside <i>galette des rois</i>,
a sweet pastry eaten on New Year's.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:25.580
Happiness comes to whoever finds it.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:29.420
What does such useless knowledge
have to do with the debut?

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:31.580
There's writing on it.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:34.630
Edward did say we should eat our sweets.

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:38.420
Maybe there are more
<i>fèves </i>in the other sweets.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:40.840
They might spell out a message.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:42.470
Nice work, Emilico!

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:44.930
Come on, let's eat!

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:50.350
All this... for the five of us?

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:54.060
I'm not eating that.
Your theory is just a wild guess.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.860
Fine, if you think you know better.

00:04:56.860 --> 00:05:00.030
But don't come crying
if your rating goes down.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:22.630
"There is a good luck charm
in the <i>galette des rois</i>."

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:25.430
But that's...

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:27.850
What are we supposed to do with that?

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:32.310
Damn it! I knew this was
just more of his abuse!

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:38.110
I ate too much. I feel sick.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:46.080
Emilico.

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:10.020
It opened!

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:13.770
This means we should go after them, right?

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:15.190
It might be a trap.

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:20.230
Besides, we don't even know
if those really are <i>fèves</i>.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:23.860
Come on, let's go!

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:28.700
Worrying about our masters
isn't a trivial matter!

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:46.550
It was supposed to be easy.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:52.680
Kate can be brought down,
no, <i>must </i>be brought down.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:56.150
But I got her living doll all fired up.

00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:57.310
On top of that,

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:03.190
when I played piano to calm myself,
Patrick and his doll start dancing!

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:08.320
Now Kate and her doll are closer,
making it harder to eliminate them!

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:12.240
This debut is a test
of my skill as a judge.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:15.620
I will seem less than
motivated if no one fails.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:19.000
But I can't simply fail
a pair without reason.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:22.590
I must get my plan back on track!

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:29.010
Calm yourself, Edward.
It really isn't that difficult.

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:32.890
That took longer than I'd thought.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:36.810
Aren't you forgetting something important?

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:39.190
Where are our shadow masters?

00:07:39.190 --> 00:07:41.320
The rules are simple.

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:44.940
You must exit the garden
before the allotted time expires.

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:47.150
But first, you must save your masters.

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:50.030
Save them? What have you done?

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:53.540
You must be concerned.
It's important to feel that way.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.870
After all, living dolls exist
for the sake of their masters.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:59.790
Why are you putting us through this?!

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:02.630
Such questions are trivial, immaterial!

00:08:02.630 --> 00:08:06.220
Consider carefully what
you should be thinking about

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:08.090
and what you should not be.

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:11.470
You must protect your masters,
for they are nobles.

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:15.890
No harm must come to a living
doll's face while in the labyrinth.

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:19.140
And a shadow's attire must not get dirty.

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:24.900
Thus far, the ranking from
the top is Lou, Shaun, Ricky, Rum,

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.150
and last, Emilico.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:30.950
Higher rankings yield a greater advantage.

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:35.950
The items you see over there
may prove useful in this test.

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:39.330
The top-ranked doll chooses first.

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:47.510
Why choose a rock over one of those items?

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:49.430
Huh?

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:52.180
I'll take this.

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:54.220
That's how you choose?!

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:56.470
I have trouble making up my mind.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:58.600
Don't neglect important decisions.

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:02.150
But it's not like you have
the capacity for regret.

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:07.480
It's not my style to carry junk around.

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.360
What is my style?

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:13.820
It could be trouble if she
threatens me with those shears.

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:16.410
Should I choose that weapon?

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:19.200
I need something really versatile.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:20.790
Water.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:25.090
Does that mean we'll
have to deal with scorches?

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:26.300
Bread.

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:29.720
This won't be over today?
We're in for a long haul?

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:33.050
Hurry up and choose.
You two are ranked the same.

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:36.680
You can decide who picks first.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:39.180
All right, I'll go first.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:40.770
Like hell you will!

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:42.690
You got some nerve!

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:50.490
You better stop messing with me.

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:56.830
You already punched me once.
Shall we pick up where we left off?

00:09:56.830 --> 00:10:01.910
Um, why don't you say what you
want to choose at the same time?

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:04.000
There's but one choice!

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:07.380
--The magnifying glass!
--The soot suit!

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:13.470
Isn't that wonderful, you two?

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:21.060
Next is Rum.

00:10:30.530 --> 00:10:34.030
A lantern during the day? That's stupid.

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:40.490
Ricky, you talk tough, but you
chose something to protect yourself.

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:45.710
Didn't you hear the rules?
No harm must come to a living doll's face.

00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:47.460
And last, Emilico.

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:49.800
Hurray! What I want is still there.

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:52.710
I know you're lying.
There's only junk left!

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:55.930
Junk? What about that bread?!

00:10:55.930 --> 00:10:59.600
You're still thinking
about food after all we ate?

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:01.970
Bread... That's no surprise.

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:06.600
Sorry, bread, not this time.

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:10.190
This is what I wanted!

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:13.490
She's an even bigger idiot than I thought!

00:11:13.490 --> 00:11:16.110
Emilico, why'd you pick that?

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:17.870
It looks heavy.

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:22.700
I had to have this!

00:11:26.420 --> 00:11:31.590
The sootglass takes about two hours
for the soot to go from bottom to top.

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:35.470
You must bring your master
to the exit before then.

00:11:35.470 --> 00:11:40.010
Take this and wait at the entrance
I told each of you to go to.

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:48.650
Now, go!

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:58.200
A pencil, rope, scissors,
a handkerchief, and a map.

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:05.200
This mark looks like a small hut.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:09.370
Hmm? What's this black dot?

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:13.920
Oh, there are five of them.
Is that where the shadow masters are?

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:17.630
Is that writing?

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:19.300
Must be a hint!

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:24.680
The magnifying glass was a smart move!
Maybe I can pinpoint my master's location.

00:12:26.980 --> 00:12:30.100
I can't read it even with this.

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:34.440
Emilico has sharp eyes.
Maybe she could read it.

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:43.990
Rum! What a coincidence!

00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:49.250
Just kidding!
My entrance was next to yours,

00:12:49.250 --> 00:12:52.790
so I thought I might run
into you if came this way.

00:12:55.130 --> 00:12:57.380
Me, too.

00:12:59.220 --> 00:13:01.970
Have you decided where to go?

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:09.770
I'm heading for this hut mark
nearby. Let's go together!

00:13:16.070 --> 00:13:17.740
Hm?

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:21.450
I'll be right back.

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:27.950
There's a waterway below!

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:33.080
I must pay more attention.
I nearly fell in.

00:13:34.840 --> 00:13:37.670
Let's put it on the map.

00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:47.350
Isn't this kind of fun?

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:59.150
I really could've used that lantern.

00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:27.970
Hush.

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:33.850
Seriously? You cut a shortcut through
the hedge?! Is that even allowed?

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:39.150
Wait. I might be able to
use her to my advantage.

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:41.490
Lou, where are you headed?

00:14:41.490 --> 00:14:42.530
Nowhere special.

00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:45.910
Your utter lack of thought is impressive.

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:48.620
I think I know where
the shadow masters are.

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:49.330
No, you don't.

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:52.620
Yes, I do! There's a hint
right on the map.

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:53.500
What map?

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:56.130
Look in the bag we received!

00:14:56.130 --> 00:15:00.880
The map has dots that seem worthless.
I'm the only one who noticed!

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:06.180
I'll take you there if
you hack us a shortcut.

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:09.050
Okay, tell me where to start.

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:10.560
However...

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:15.230
I'll give you a buzz cut if you're lying.

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:18.940
It's a deal!

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:29.580
You can put your stuff in here.

00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:30.740
Oh, um...

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:32.160
Go ahead.

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:55.980
I'm fine.

00:15:55.980 --> 00:15:59.350
See? I can even push it with one hand.

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:10.370
That was scary!

00:16:10.370 --> 00:16:12.660
But at least it stopped.

00:16:16.790 --> 00:16:20.040
Don't worry. I don't need help.

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:23.000
That was my fault.

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:31.890
All right!

00:16:38.140 --> 00:16:41.440
I want to help.

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:50.660
We can push it up if we work together.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:17:00.120
I was trying to be strong.

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:12.050
We can get more done by working together!

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:32.200
We made it!

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:39.410
Nice work!

00:17:43.630 --> 00:17:45.630
An explosion?!

00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:48.340
Did someone trigger a trap?

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:53.800
Soot really packs a punch.

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:04.770
The air is so refreshing.

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:08.230
A stroll might be nice.

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:15.070
This place is huge!

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:18.490
We can see all sorts
of things from up here.

00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:25.790
Is that... soot?

00:18:33.930 --> 00:18:36.890
There are little black dots here.

00:18:36.890 --> 00:18:40.390
I know! These are where
the shadow masters are!

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:44.900
This dot is nearby. Let's go have a look!

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:53.950
I'll pick a few more
oranges for Mistress Kate.

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:04.330
Edward said wait here
till someone comes, but...

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:10.130
Maybe this soot power could help.

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:16.010
Or is it risky drawing attention to it?

00:19:16.010 --> 00:19:17.930
It is so tempting, though.

00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:20.470
Oh, it's you, Kate.

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:22.600
That's an interesting spot.

00:19:22.600 --> 00:19:23.520
John!

00:19:23.520 --> 00:19:28.270
This is perfect.
There's a question that cannot wait.

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:30.940
John wants your hand in marriage!

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:32.940
Not a chance.

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:36.320
Don't be so hasty.
John has taken a fancy to you.

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:39.320
He shall be King of Shadows House.

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:41.200
You will not regret this.

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:44.040
What's with him? Is he an utter fool?

00:19:44.040 --> 00:19:47.290
Are you saying you'll help
if we're to be married?

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:50.340
Kate will not marry
someone so calculating.

00:19:50.340 --> 00:19:53.090
Yes, that was the plan.

00:19:53.090 --> 00:19:56.260
Quite perceptive.
You are the one for John.

00:19:56.260 --> 00:19:59.180
I wish he'd go away already.

00:19:59.180 --> 00:20:01.680
John was put in a crate,

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:06.100
but with a wham, bang, kaboom,
he blew it to bits and escaped!

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:10.190
If you overcome this ordeal
on your own, we'll be equals.

00:20:10.190 --> 00:20:13.570
Then we may revisit the subject.

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:16.650
Wait. Didn't Shaun help you escape?

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:20.320
No, John did it without
anyone else's help.

00:20:20.320 --> 00:20:21.280
How?

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:25.620
Weren't you listening?
It was like, wham, bang, kaboom!

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:29.500
It doesn't appear he was
consciously controlling soot.

00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:31.290
But in your case...

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:37.050
that cage is quite a sight to see.

00:20:37.050 --> 00:20:39.680
It looks more challenging
than John's crate.

00:20:39.680 --> 00:20:43.640
How will Shaun find you if
you're not where you should be?

00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:47.940
Oh, right. We were told to wait.
Shaun was supposed to come?

00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:50.190
So that's it. You're a smart one, Kate.

00:20:50.190 --> 00:20:54.690
Goodbye for now. Call John really
loud if you wish to be saved.

00:20:57.570 --> 00:21:01.490
There were no repercussions
for his conspicuous use of soot.

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:03.160
Good to know.

00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:08.790
And it's good to know that there are
other shadows who can control soot.

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:12.040
This whole test is like one big spectacle.

00:21:13.130 --> 00:21:15.170
This debut...

00:21:15.170 --> 00:21:19.300
It's as if someone were watching us.

00:21:24.470 --> 00:21:28.100
It seems John failed
to throw Kate off-kilter.

00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:33.020
But his high soot volume
was quite impressive.

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:36.730
Epic failures are more entertaining
than outstanding candidates.

00:21:36.730 --> 00:21:39.900
What vulgar tastes you have.
This is a test.

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:43.240
Oh, please. It is one of
the few diversions we have.

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:48.120
John and that labyrinth-chopping
doll are most entertaining.

00:21:48.120 --> 00:21:52.420
But Edward went through such
pains to create it, the poor fellow.

00:21:52.420 --> 00:21:57.130
Does he mean to be a gardener?
His obstinate personality is clear to see.

00:21:57.130 --> 00:21:59.010
Should you not say, earnest?

00:21:59.010 --> 00:22:03.340
He is trying to please
Lord Grandfather, no doubt.

00:22:03.340 --> 00:22:07.350
In any case, Edward's bias in
regards to the test is unflattering.

00:22:07.350 --> 00:22:10.680
Notably, his treatment
of poor last-place Kate.

00:22:11.730 --> 00:22:16.820
Even worse, her living doll
has sunshine on the brain.

00:23:48.700 --> 00:23:51.870
Next episode, "An Incomplete Map."

00:23:48.780 --> 00:23:51.990
NEXT EPISODE

00:23:48.780 --> 00:23:51.990
An Incomplete Map
